  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Black Quotidian: Everyday History in African-American Newspapers (2019), published by Stanford University Press, has been cited 10 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Black Quotidian: Everyday History in African-American Newspapers by Matthew F. Delmont was published by Stanford University Press in 2019. Conceptually, the work connects to Newspaper, History, Geography, Ethnology and Genealogy. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) — Multimodal.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 10 citations. Citations peaked in 2023 with 8 citing works. Notable citing venues include Bloomsbury Academic eBooks. The citing works include 7 book chapters and 1 report. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">No teaching use or download figures have been recorded for it yet.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 2 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
